{
  "schema_version": "2",
  "data_version": "0.1.0",
  "purpose": "Shared cross-language conformance vectors for EideticLib. Both the Swift and Rust implementations of lookup() MUST produce these outputs for the given inputs. Any divergence is a hard conformance failure.",
  "notes": [
    "expected_code values are FDC (Frame-Directed Classification) codes produced by LatticeLib's FDC.encode / Fdc::encode. They are NOT UDC (Universal Decimal Classification) codes.",
    "schema_version 1 contained a mistake: expected_code was named expected_udc and populated with UDC codes from a different classification system. Version 2 corrects this to real FDC codes verified against both Swift and Rust engines.",
    "expected_qid values are Wikidata Q-IDs returned by FDC.encodeAnchor as the dominant concept Q-ID in the bag.",
    "Tests assert code and wikidata_qid equality. Confidence and data_version are not part of the conformance contract.",
    "Cases with empty expected_code AND null expected_qid are UNRESOLVED cases where the encoder produces no answer (no signature overlap).",
    "Cases with populated expected_code and null expected_qid are cases where the bag contains no Wikidata Q-ID concept."
  ],
